    "sections": [
      {
        "label": "1st period",
        "score": "BOS 0, NYR 0",
        "text": "David Pastrnak, named the team's 28th captain the week before, got a big ovation before puck drop. The opening period was scoreless: Boston killed an early Rangers power play and came up empty on one of its own."
      },
      {
        "label": "2nd period",
        "score": "BOS 0, NYR 0",
        "text": "Still 0–0 after 40 minutes. Igor Shesterkin denied Fraser Minten on a 2-on-1, and Nikita Zadorov and Matt Rempe nearly dropped the gloves. Jeremy Swayman had 15 saves through two periods, Shesterkin 14."
      },
      {
        "label": "3rd period",
        "score": "Final: BOS 3, NYR 0",
        "text": "The Rangers pushed early, and Swayman stopped Pavel Dorofeyev and J.T. Miller in succession at 9:05; Pavel Zacha hit the post at the other end. With 3:46 left, Minten beat Shesterkin from the slot for a 1–0 lead. Fifty-two seconds later JJ Peterka, in his Bruins debut, stickhandled between Braden Schneider's legs and scored for 2–0, and Mark Kastelic hit the empty net 23 seconds after that for 3–0."
      }
    ],
